.                                 * In the original variable, higher shares mea
> n less equality.
.                                 * Hence, coef. for daughter should be negativ
> e.
.                                 * We reverse the coding so that coef. can be 
> interpreted in line with hypothesis
.                                 * I.e., positive coef. -> greater gender equa
> lity in the household
.         
.         
.         *       As explained in our PAP we consider the treatment and control
>  to be "having one daughter" and "having one son". 
. 
.         * Daughter dummy
